#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# get

#% text
# `get(file)` reads back the value that `put(value, file)` wrote to a file.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The file holds the value in input form after a first line `#! mathcas 2 value`; it can be read and edited as text.

#% item
# Machine reals are written with the digits that read back to the same number, so a value comes back exactly.

#% item
# A solution of `n_dsolve` is written as an `interpolation` through its values at 16 points per step (at least 2049 points), so it can be read in a later session; it is then a cubic spline through the solution.

#% item
# `get` evaluates the value again in the session that reads it.

#% item
# A file that cannot be written or read gives `failure(io, file, message)`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# Save a list and read it back:

#% cell
file = string_join(temporary_directory(), "values.mx"); put([1/3, 0.1 + 0.2, "text", x -> 2], file); get(file)
#% output
#= [1/3, 0.30000000000000004, "text", x -> 2]

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Save the solution of a differential equation and use it again without solving:

#% cell
sol = n_dsolve([y'(t) == -y(t), y(0) == 1], y, [t, 0, 1]); string_ends(put(sol, string_join(temporary_directory(), "sol.mx")), "sol.mx")
#% output
#= true

#% cell
s = get(string_join(temporary_directory(), "sol.mx")); [y(0.5), y'(0.5)] /. s
#% output
#= [0.6065306602814926, -0.6065306532938289]

#% cell
(y(0.5) /. s) - exp(-0.5)
#% output
#= 5.688591819819067e-10

#% text
# Interpolations, associations and arrays are kept as they are:

#% cell
v = assoc("table" -> interpolation([1, 4, 9, 16]), "m" -> [[1.5, 2], [3, 4]]); put(v, string_join(temporary_directory(), "assoc.mx")); get(string_join(temporary_directory(), "assoc.mx")) == v
#% output
#= true

#% subsection
# Possible issues

#% text
# The file name must be a string:

#% cell
put([1, 2], 3)
#% output
#! failure(argument, put, 2)

#% text
# A file that does not exist gives `failure(io, file, message)`, with the system's message:

#% cell
failure_tag(get("no such file.mx"))
#% output
#= io

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `put`, `export_data`, `import_data`, `to_string`, `to_expression`, `n_dsolve`, `interpolation`
